To verify the correctness of the inserted code, we could use a test method as follows:

```cs
[TestMethod]
public void TestArrayListAdd()
{
    int x = 1;
    int y = 2;
    ArrayList al = new ArrayList();
    Assert.AreEqual(1, al.Count, "Initially the ArrayList should have one element");
    for (int i = 0; i < y; i++)
    {
        x.Inc(1);
    }
    al.Add(x);
    Assert.AreEqual(2, al.Count, "After adding x, the ArrayList should have two elements");
    Assert.AreEqual(3, al[1], "After adding x, the ArrayList's value should be 3");
}
```
The comment "@@@ Value of x increases by y in the function" indicates that after the loop for incrementing x by y, the value of x should increase by y in the ArrayList object. We add x to the ArrayList al in the TestArrayListAdd function and then perform the Assertions to verify that x is indeed added to the ArrayList al. After adding x to the ArrayList, the Count of al should be 2, and the second element of al should be 3 (x + y).--------------------